<title>USA: Bristol to buy Bass Holiday Inns - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Bristol to buy Bass Holiday Inns - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>In a transaction that would make Bristol Hotel Co one of the largest independent hotel owner-operators in the U.S., Bristol agreed to buy from Bass Plc its Holiday Inn hotels in the U.S. for $650 million to $670 million in cash and stock, The Wall Street Journal reported Monday.</p>
<p>Bass, the Holiday Inn franchiser world-wide, will sell its roughly 60 Holiday Inns in the U.S. and retain its more up-scale Crown Plaza hotels, the story says.</p>
<p>Bristol currently owns 39 hotels in seven states, the story says.</p>
